        ],
        "bhavartha": "Kālabhairava shines like ten million suns. He carries (us) across the ocean of worldly life, and He is the Supreme. His throat is blue, He gives what we long for, and He has three eyes. He is Death even to Death, His eyes are like lotuses, He holds a rosary and the trident, and He never perishes. The singer worships Him: Kālabhairava, the supreme lord of the city of Kāśī."
      },
      "hi": {
